    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204789": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Housing and Data",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Housing and Data SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Housing and Data Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Housing and Data Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residential Experience and Housing Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 14, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $57,151.00 - $62,000.00 Position ID: 204789 Share Job Description: SUNY Oneonta is seeking a community development focused leader to join our team as Assistant Director of Housing and Data . The Assistant Director reports directly to the Director of Residence Life and Housing and functions under a flexible work schedule that may include weekend and evening hours. Residence Life and Housing fosters an inclusive environment for growth and learning; provides high-quality facilities, services, and programs; and supports student academic success and retention. Our goals are to build a residential program that fosters a spirit of engagement and community among students, staff, and faculty, to foster a sense of belonging to the residential community through student engagement and leadership in governance, and to promote student academic success. The Office of On Campus Housing and Residence Life is under the Residential Experience and Housing Department, which also houses offices of Move-In, Orientation and Welcome; as well as the Office of Off Campus and Commuter Students. Our office works closely with many other areas of the University through committee work, collaboration, and resource sharing. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/residential-experience-and-housing . Duties may include: Supervision of 4-6 Residence Hall Directors. Oversight of the occupancy program for 3,000 bed campus. Design and execution of new and returning housing application and assignment processes. Management of room changes. Administration of residential damage billing process. Assistance with furniture procurement and renovation planning. Maintenance and administration of the housing database StarRez. Assistance with card access system. Design and distribution of weekly reports for the department, division, and university stakeholders. Assistance in compiling and analyzing historic and current occupancy data to inform occupancy projections. Serving as department liaison with Student Accounts and Dining Services as it relates to student bills. Participation in on call duty rotation. Assistance with emergency/crisis management for the department. Chairing department committees. Salary: $57,151- $62,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. One (1) year or more experience supervising, evaluating, and selecting staff. Experience managing building occupancy. Experience with emergencies or crisis response (duty rotation). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience with excel spreadsheets or other data management systems. Preferred: Master's degree in Higher Education Administration or related field. Experience with StarRez or similar occupancy database systems. Experience with card access management systems. Experience working with housing accommodations. Ability to work effectively under pressure and meet established goals and objectives. Ability to work independently and take initiative on projects. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/mission-values-vision/inclusivity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=204789 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205231": {
      "title": "Workforce Development Coordinator",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Workforce Development Coordinator SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Workforce Development Coordinator Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Workforce Development Coordinator Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Type: Full-time Temporary Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $57,151.00 - $57,151.00 Position ID: 205231 Share Job Description: The Workforce Development Coordinator serves as a key member of the Extended and Community Learning (ExCL) Center team and is responsible for the planning, coordination, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of workforce development and continuing education initiatives that support regional economic development and lifelong learning. This position serves as an ambassador for SUNY Oneonta and the ExCL Center by fostering strategic partnerships that advance workforce development, career readiness, adult education, and economic mobility throughout the region. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/academics/extended-learning . Duties May Include: Developing, implementing, administering, and evaluating workforce development, continuing education, professional development, apprenticeship, certificate, customized training, and grant-funded programs that support the mission of the ExCL Center and SUNY Oneonta. Building and maintaining collaborative relationships with employers, workforce development agencies, government organizations, educational institutions, workforce investment partners, economic development organizations, and community stakeholders to identify workforce needs, develop responsive training solutions, and expand educational opportunities throughout the region. Coordinating all aspects of workforce programming, including program logistics, scheduling, facilities, technology, registration, instructional materials, purchasing, contracts, learner support services, and the recruitment and support of instructors, subject matter experts, and training partners. Managing multiple projects simultaneously while monitoring program quality, participant outcomes, timelines, deliverables, compliance requirements, and performance metrics; collecting and reporting data and recommending improvements to enhance program effectiveness and operational efficiency. Providing exceptional customer service and learner support throughout recruitment, enrollment, training participation, program completion, and credential attainment while utilizing student information systems, customer relationship management platforms, learning management systems, and other enterprise technologies to support program operations. Conducting outreach, researching workforce and labor market trends, and representing the ExCL Center and SUNY Oneonta at employer visits, workforce summits, career fairs, conferences, advisory boards, community meetings, networking events, and other activities that advance workforce development initiatives and institutional priorities. Performing work in a dynamic environment requiring independent judgment, collaboration with internal and external stakeholders, occasional evening and weekend hours, local travel, and attendance at off-site meetings and events. Salary: $57,151. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Minimum of three (3) years of experience in program management, workforce development, community engagement, nonprofit administration, training coordination, or a closely related field. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple programs, projects, deadlines, and competing priorities simultaneously. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and other technology platforms used to support program administration and operations. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Valid driver's license at time of appointment. Preferred: Experience working in workforce development, economic development, adult education, or a related field. Experience developing, implementing, administering, and evaluating educational, workforce development, training, or grant-funded programs. Experience building partnerships with employers, workforce agencies, community organizations, educational institutions, and other external stakeholders. Experience using student information systems, customer relationship management (CRM) platforms, registration systems, learning management systems, or similar technologies (e.g., Banner, Slate, Salesforce). Knowledge of workforce development practices, labor market trends, adult learning principles, enrollment management, and regional workforce needs. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205231 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Application Instructions: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205293": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Elementary Education and Reading",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Lecturer of Elementary Education and Reading SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Lecturer of Elementary Education and Reading Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Lecturer of Elementary Education and Reading Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Elementary Education and Reading Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 28, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $50,063.00 - $50,063.00 Position ID: 205293 Share Job Description: Grounded in the belief that all children can learn, SUNY Oneonta's Department of Elementary Education and Reading seeks a Lecturer with an emphasis on Early Childhood Education , beginning Fall 2027 to help advance this mission. Expectations include, but are not limited to, teaching, student engagement, service, engagement with community colleges and regional schools, and continuing professional development. This is an on-campus position. SUNY Oneonta is recognized as a regional leader in teacher education and is a member in good standing of the Association for Advancing Quality in Educator Preparation (AAQEP). The Department of Elementary Education and Reading is the largest on campus, with 14 faculty members and a wide range of programs: Undergraduate degrees in Childhood Education (1-6) and Early Childhood/Childhood Education (B-6), and graduate degrees in Literacy Education (Birth-12. Faculty expertise includes literacy education, rural teacher preparation, social justice education, and experiential learning. The department is also engaged in university-school district collaborations and community college 2+2 partnerships that create innovative programming opportunities. To learn more about the University or the Department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/elementary-education-and-reading . Duties include but are not limited to: Teaching undergraduate courses in early childhood and childhood education methods, foundational education courses, graduate literacy education courses, and other areas as needed by the department. Teaching in multiple modalities, including in-person and online. Working collaboratively with departmental and school colleagues. Partnering with local school districts and supervision of students on site. Contributing to university-wide goals and initiatives. Engaging with the department, school, university, and community endeavors. Salary: $50,063. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Master's Degree in Education or closely related field. Teaching certification and a minimum of three years teaching at the elementary or middle school level. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively. Demonstrated commitment to student-ready pedagogies. Demonstrated interest in and commitment to the role of service in an academic career. Strong commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and social justice, with particular attention to supporting first-generation college students and community college transfer students. Strong commitment to engaging in field-based partnerships. Preferred: Relevant college teaching experience (B-2 methods). Experience with social-emotional teaching and learning. Experience or a demonstrated interest in non-traditional grading approaches. Experience teaching face-to-face, online or hybrid (partially online) courses. Experience or demonstrated interest in culturally relevant teaching pedagogies and/or multicultural teaching. Experience working with non-traditional and/or diverse student populations and within community college partnership programs. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205293 . Please upload a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, copies of graduate transcripts (official required at time of appointment), copies of your teaching certificate, a statement of teaching philosophy, a research statement, and a diversity statement that reflects an evidence-based commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, social justice, and access to higher education. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205247": {
      "title": "Senior Financial Analyst",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Senior Financial Analyst SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Senior Financial Analyst Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Financial Analyst Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Budget Office Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 28, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $65,000.00 - $75,000.00 Position ID: 205247 Share Job Description: The Budget Office at the State University of New York (SUNY) Oneonta seeks a Senior Financial Analyst to serve as a senior analytical resource within the Budget Office. Reporting to the Director of University Budget & Financial Planning, the position plays a key role in supporting the University's financial operations, planning efforts, and process improvement initiatives through data-driven analysis and strategic decision support. The successful candidate will provide advanced financial analysis and decision-support services to University leadership and will be responsible for monitoring and analyzing budget activity across all University funds. This position independently identifies financial trends, investigates discrepancies, develops recommendations, and supports institutional planning, resource allocation, and long-term fiscal sustainability. The incumbent will also lead and support process improvement initiatives, workflow enhancements, and reporting solutions that increase operational efficiency, strengthen internal controls, and reduce duplicate data entry. The Budget Office provides leadership and support for the University's budget planning, monitoring, financial reporting, and resource allocation functions. The office develops and administers budgets across University funds, including the State Core Operating Budget (Revenue Offset), Dormitory Income Fund Reimbursable (DIFR), General Income Fund Reimbursable (IFR), Summer Session, and Tuition Overflow (SUTRA). The office works closely with SUNY System Administration, campus leadership, and affiliated organizations to support strategic planning, informed decision-making, and long-term fiscal sustainability. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/university-offices/budget-office . Duties may include: Perform complex budget and financial analysis across all University funds and funding sources. Develop financial reports, dashboards, forecasts, projections, and decision-support tools for University leadership. Monitor budget activity, revenues, expenditures, allocations, and fund balances; identifying trends, discrepancies, risks, and opportunities for improvement. Independently research and resolve budget and financial discrepancies and recommend corrective actions. Support annual budget development, resource allocation, financial planning, and forecasting activities. Manage and monitor Temporary Services (TS) budgets, including review, reconciliation, forecasting, and analysis. Coordinate fiscal year-end and fiscal year start-up activities, including allocation transfers, expenditure transfers, reporting, segregation balance monitoring, and Form 1 development. Lead continuous improvement initiatives focused on increasing efficiency, improving data integrity, strengthening internal controls, and reducing duplicate data entry. Develop and enhance budget reporting systems, dashboards, business intelligence tools, and automated workflows. Provide guidance and consultation to campus departments regarding budget policies, financial management practices, resource planning, and budget-related issues. Prepare and present financial analyses, recommendations, and reports to University leadership and campus stakeholders. Ensure compliance with University, SUNY, and New York State financial policies, procedures, and reporting requirements. Salary: $65,000- $75,000 - commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field. Minimum of four (4) years of progressively responsible experience in budgeting, budget development, forecasting, financial reporting, budget control, financial modeling, analytical decision support, financial analysis, financial planning, accounting, or related financial administration functions. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel. Demonstrated ability to analyze complex financial information and communicate findings effectively to both financial and non-financial audiences. Additional: Demonstrated analytical, problem-solving, and critical-thinking skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to collaborate effectively with stakeholders across multiple organizational levels. Demonstrated support of an inclusive and welcoming workplace environment. Preferred: Master's degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a related field. Experience in higher education, New York State government, or other public-sector organizations. Experience with business intelligence platforms, dashboards, financial reporting tools, and data analytics systems. Experience leading process improvement, workflow redesign, or automation initiatives. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/mission-values-vision/inclusivity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205247 Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205333": {
      "title": "Student Belonging and Success Specialist",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Student Belonging and Success Specialist SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Student Belonging and Success Specialist Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Belonging and Success Specialist Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Office of Equity and Inclusion Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $60,245.00 - $60,245.00 Position ID: 205333 Share Job Description: The Student Belonging and Success Specialist is a student-facing professional within the Office of Equity and Inclusion who partners closely with the Office of Academic Success & Achievement to advance student success through the Academic Momentum (AcMo) Campus Plan. The position focuses on students whose persistence may be influenced by barriers related to belonging, inclusion, campus connection, identity, and other non-academic experiences that affect their ability to thrive at SUNY Oneonta. Working collaboratively with the Academic Success & Retention Program Coordinator and the Academic Success & Retention Program Associate, the Specialist provides belonging-centered outreach to students referred through institutional student success processes and assists in developing strategies to support student populations identified through the AcMo Campus Plan. The Specialist collaborates with Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, and other campus partners to strengthen students' connection to the university and support institutional efforts focused on retention, persistence, and student success. The position serves as the Office of Equity and Inclusion's primary liaison with Academic Affairs regarding belonging-centered student success initiatives. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/office-equity-and-inclusion . Duties May Include: Belonging-Centered Student Outreach (30%) Providing individualized outreach to students whose persistence may be influenced by barriers related to belonging, inclusion, campus connection, or other non-academic experiences. Conducting outreach to students referred through the University's student success processes. Meeting individually with students to better understand experiences affecting their sense of belonging and connection to the university. Engaging students in conversations that identify strengths, challenges, and opportunities for strengthening their connection to the institution. Collaborating with students to develop individualized strategies that foster belonging and support persistence. Maintaining appropriate follow-up with students and coordinating, when appropriate, with campus partners supporting the student's success. Inclusive Student Success Strategies (30%) Partnering with the Office of Academic Success & Achievement to ensure outreach efforts intentionally support students whose experiences may require additional attention from a belonging and inclusion perspective. Collaborating with the Academic Success & Retention Program Coordinator on outreach strategies for students referred through Navigate and other institutional processes when belonging-related concerns are identified. Partnering with the Academic Success & Retention Program Associate to develop outreach initiatives for student populations identified through the Academic Momentum Campus Plan. Contributing to planning outreach strategies that strengthen students' connection to the university. Assisting in evaluating the effectiveness of outreach efforts and recommending improvements. Supervising Office of Equity and Inclusion interns. Coordinating the Dragons of Excellence Program. Campus Collaboration (25%) Serving as the Office of Equity and Inclusion's primary liaison with Academic Affairs regarding belonging-centered student success initiatives. Collaborating with Academic Affairs and other campus partners to support coordinated student success efforts. Providing consultation regarding belonging and inclusion considerations during the development of student success initiatives. Assisting in coordinating collaborative outreach activities involving multiple campus partners. Participating in committees and working groups supporting student success and inclusive excellence. Coordinating the Red Dragon Games. Serving on the Bias Acts Response Team. Assessment and Continuous Improvement (15%) Supporting institutional efforts to better understand how belonging influences student persistence. Documenting outreach activities and student engagement outcomes. Identifying recurring themes and barriers affecting students' experiences. Sharing observations that may inform future AcMo initiatives. Contributing to assessment and continuous improvement efforts related to student belonging and persistence. Salary: $60,245. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. At least two years of professional experience in higher education, student support services, diversity and inclusion, student affairs, academic affairs, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to build supportive relationships with students from diverse backgrounds. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive excellence and student success. Preferred: Master's degree. Experience supporting student persistence, belonging, or student success initiatives. Experience conducting individualized outreach or student support. Familiarity with factors influencing student persistence in higher education. Experience working collaboratively across multiple institutional units. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205333 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205366": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Director for Employee Services Category: Management / Confidential Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Employee Services Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $90,000.00 - $95,000.00 Position ID: 205366 Share Job Description: People are at the heart of everything we do. As Assistant/Associate Director of Employee Services , you'll help employees, supervisors, and campus leaders navigate complex workplace situations, strengthen working relationships, and support a positive and productive university community. Working closely with the Chief Human Resources Officer (CHRO), you'll have the opportunity to lead or provide guidance on employee and labor relations matters, payroll and benefits administration, performance management, workplace conflict resolution, training and development, and compliance. Employee Services at SUNY Oneonta is dedicated to supporting the growth and success of every member of our campus community. Through partnership, problem-solving, and responsive service, the department strives to offer an exceptional employee experience while supporting individual success and advancing the University's mission. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/university-offices/employee-services . Duties May Include: Provide leadership, supervision, mentoring, and performance management for assigned Employee Services team members. Establish priorities, coordinate workflows, and support the effective delivery of various employee related services. Contribute to departmental projects, initiatives, and continuous improvement efforts. Conduct workplace investigations and support disciplinary processes in accordance with established policies, procedures, and applicable collective bargaining agreements. Provide consultation and guidance to supervisors and employees on a wide range of employee relations matters such as performance management, workplace concerns and policy interpretation. Resolve workplace conflicts by facilitating discussions, recommending solutions, and ensuring issues are handled with fairness and confidentiality. Develop and deliver training in partnership with the CHRO on leadership, employee relations, performance management, workplace expectations, and policy and regulatory compliance. Build and guide processes for employment-related functions such as benefits, payroll, and recruitment administration. Exercise exceptional judgment and uphold the highest standards of ethics, professionalism, discretion, and confidentiality when handling sensitive and complex matters. Salary: $90,000 - $95,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited institution. Minimum of 6 years' progressive Human Resources experience, with at least 4 years' HR experience at the mid/high management level, leading, supervising, or coordinating the work of other human resources staff members. Demonstrated experience conducting workplace investigations. Highly effective written and oral communication skills. Impeccable confidentiality and ethical standards. Additional : Strong knowledge of HR best practices, employment law, and compliance requirements. Evidence of outstanding cultural competency and working successfully with employees from varied backgrounds in the workplace. Deep experience with employee relations and sensitive workplace matters. Extensive knowledge of, and ability to understand and apply employment laws, regulations, policies, and collective bargaining agreements. Preferred: Current PHR/SPHR, SHRM-CP/SHRM-SCP, or similar HR certification. Master's degree in human resources, business administration, social sciences, labor relations, public administration, or other related discipline. Experience supporting payroll and/or benefits administration. Experience developing and delivering employee related training programs. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205366 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For full consideration, applications should be submitted by October 10, 2026 . For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205430": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Developmental Psychology",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Developmental Psychology SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Developmental Psychology Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Developmental Psychology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Oct 1, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $64,890.00 - $64,890.00 Position ID: 205430 Share Job Description: The Department of Psychology at the State University of New York at Oneonta invites applications for a tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor of Developmental Psychology beginning Fall 2027 . Expectations include, but are not limited to, teaching, research, student advisement, university service, and continuing professional development. This position reports directly to the Chair of the Department of Psychology. The Department of Psychology at the State University of New York at Oneonta is a thriving department of 11 full-time faculty members with diverse research interests that create an engaging learning environment characterized by accessible faculty, teamwork, student research opportunities, and technology-supported classrooms. The department is committed to providing a solid knowledge base in psychology, fostering scientific inquiry and critical thinking skills, promoting competence in written and oral communication, and supporting ethical and social responsibility in a diverse world. We value experience working with diverse populations, inclusive teaching pedagogies, and multicultural teaching experiences that support students' overall professional development. The department is part of the School of Sciences, which consists of 10 academic departments and nearly 2,000 students majoring in 20 programs. To learn more about the University and the Department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ and https://suny.oneonta.edu/psychology . Duties include but are not limited to: Teach courses in developmental psychology and develop courses in area of specialization. Maintain an active research program. Participate in student involvements such as advisement, research supervision, and mentoring. Provide service to the department and university. Salary: $64,890. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Doctorate Degree in Developmental Psychology, or a closely related discipline. ABD considered; official confirmation of degree conferral by issuing institution by start of employment. Ability to initiate and sustain a suitable research program.?Specialization in late adulthood/aging, geropsychology, or gerontology in both teaching and research. Ability to teach online. Additional Qualifications: Experience teaching developmental courses in aging, geropsychology, gerontology, end-of-lifestudies or similar areas. Preferred Qualifications: Ability to teach courses in the core areas of our curriculum, especially research methods and statistics. Evidence of teaching effectiveness, capability of initiating a suitable and productive research program, and scholarly productivity. Demonstrated experience involving undergraduate students in research. Experience advising and mentoring undergraduate students. Experience in teaching, mentoring, research, or service with diverse and/or multicultural populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205430 . Please upload letter of interest, curriculum vitae, transcripts, statement of teaching philosophy, and statement of research interests. Please include course evaluations if available. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205813": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Comparative Politics and International Relations",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor in Comparative Politics and International Relations SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor in Comparative Politics and International Relations Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor in Comparative Politics and International Relations Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Political Science Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $64,890.00 - $64,890.00 Position ID: 205813 Share Job Description: For those who study how political institutions, governments, and global relationships shape the world around us, SUNY Oneonta offers an exciting opportunity as a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Comparative Politics and International Relations . The successful candidate will join a growing and active department in the School of Liberal Arts and Business, helping students develop the critical thinking, analytical, and civic engagement skills needed to understand complex political and international issues. The Political Science Department's six full-time faculty members offer courses across the discipline in Comparative Politics, International Relations, American Politics, and Political Theory. The department is home to vibrant programs in Political Science and International Studies, providing students with opportunities to examine government, politics, and global affairs through multiple perspectives. The International Studies program is an interdisciplinary major that emphasizes experiential learning, with tracks in international development and culture & society. To learn more about the University and the Department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ and https://suny.oneonta.edu/political-science . Duties May Include: Teaching and developing courses in Comparative Politics and International Relations based on the candidate's expertise and departmental needs. Teaching introductory Global Challenges, undergraduate research methods, and a capstone seminar. Conducting research in the candidate's area of expertise. Serving on departmental and college-wide committees. Advising students. Engaging with the larger community. Salary: $64,890. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: PhD in Political Science with specialization in International Relations and/or Comparative Politics. ABD considered; official confirmation of degree conferral by issuing institution by start of employment. Undergraduate teaching experience as instructor of record. Preferred Qualifications: Ability to teach existing classes including introductory Global Challenges, undergraduate research methods, and a capstone seminar. Ability to develop new courses in two or more of the following areas: Conflict and political violence Human security Immigration Human rights Political economy Development Demonstrated potential for maintaining a research agenda that informs teaching. Interest in experiential learning opportunities such as Model United Nations or other courses that involve travel or field visits. Experience in teaching, mentoring, research, or service with diverse and/or multicultural populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205813 . Please upload letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy and (if available) teaching evaluations, a sample of scholarly work, and sample course syllabi. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205749": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Cellular & Molecular Biology and Physiology",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Cellular & Molecular Biology and Physiology SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Cellular & Molecular Biology and Physiology Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Cellular & Molecular Biology and Physiology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biology Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Oct 14, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $64,890.00 - $64,890.00 Position ID: 205749 Share Job Description: The Biology Department at the State University of New York at Oneonta is seeking someone who specializes in Cellular & Molecular Biology and Physiology to support our undergraduate program. Expectations for this tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor of Cellular & Molecular Biology and Physiology include contributing to a student-focused department through teaching, research, student advising, university and departmental service, and continuing professional development. The Biology Department offers undergraduate pathways in biomedical, cellular and molecular, ecology and evolution, and general biology, serving approximately 300 biology majors and 500 pre-health students. Faculty have opportunities to engage students in research and collaborate with colleagues across disciplines while utilizing resources that include molecular biology laboratories, BSL1 and BSL2 mammalian cell culture facilities, multifunctional microscopy, College Camp, and the Biological Field Station in nearby Cooperstown, NY. To learn more about the State University of New York (SUNY) and the department, visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ and https://suny.oneonta.edu/biology-department . Duties include but are not limited to: Teaching lectures and laboratories for undergraduate courses in introductory and upper-division cell and molecular biology. Teaching lectures and laboratories in: Pathophysiology Microbiology Physiology Engaging in research activities with students. Advising undergraduate students. Providing service to the department. Salary: $64,890.00. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: PhD in cell and molecular biology, physiology, biology, or a related area. Experience teaching biology at the undergraduate level. Evidence of effective written communication skills. Evidence of effective presentation skills. Preferred Qualifications: Research experience with emphasis in cell biology, molecular biology, or pathophysiology. Experience teaching cell and molecular biology (introductory or intermediate). Experience teaching pathophysiology, physiology, or microbiology. Experience mentoring undergraduates and/or undergraduate research. Experience as instructor of record for undergraduate-level biology courses. Experience with course design, including Course-based Undergraduate Research Experiences (CUREs). Experience working with diverse populations and/or teaching pedagogies and/or multicultural teaching experience. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205749 . Please upload your Cover letter, CV, Statement of teaching philosophy including how your work would contribute to DEI practices/pedagogies, Statement of research interests, and copies of your transcripts. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205812": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Community Standards",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Associate Director of Community Standards SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director of Community Standards Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director of Community Standards Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Community Standards Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $67,375.00 - $72,000.00 Position ID: 205812 Share Job Description: The Division of Student Affairs is committed to ensuring every student's SUNY Oneonta experience is positive, safe, healthy, and meaningful. We provide students with the tools and support they need to thrive both during their time on campus and beyond graduation. The Office of Community Standards is responsible for communicating SUNY Oneonta's behavioral expectations via the Code of Student Conduct. The office provides educational opportunities which foster student learning, personal integrity, and ethical development by holding students accountable for behavior that is not consistent with SUNY Oneonta's expectations. We are seeking an Associate Director of Community Standards to lead the department and further develop and prepare students to enter a global society while promoting healthy and safe lifestyles. This 12-month position reports to the Associate Vice President of Student Affairs, Dean of Students and involves regular engagement with students, campus partners, and community resources. The Office of Community Standards collaborates with students navigating academic and/or behavioral concerns and helps connect them to appropriate support on campus. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/office-community-standards . Duties May Include: Ensuring the investigation and adjudication of alleged violations of the Code of Student Conduct for individuals and student organizations. Overseeing annual review, revision, and distribution of the Code of Student Conduct. Coordinating the Standing Disciplinary Board hearings and appeal process. Working regularly with the Title IX Coordinator to ensure proper investigation and compliance in cases involving sexual violence, stalking, domestic violence, or dating violence are suspected. Developing and implementing a comprehensive assessment plan for the Office of Community Standards. Providing monthly and end-of-semester data reports, including retention and persistence data. Providing supervision to a Hearing Officer, Hearing Board, and Administrative Assistant. Providing training and consultation, including: Training and consultation for residence life staff, faculty, and other campus and community constituents. Training for Hearing Board members annually. Training and support for Greek Life and the Greek Life J-Board.Serving as liaison to Greek Life and the Greek Life J-Board. Serving as Chair of the Behavioral Assessment/Intervention Team (BAIT) and managing documentation and communication for team members. Serving on campus committees and work groups. Serving as a resource for campus and community constituents regarding conflict resolution. Maintaining records in accordance with FERPA, NYS, and SUNY Oneonta's requirements. Participating in activities and collaborating with other offices within the Division of Student Affairs. Salary: $67,375 - $72,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Higher Education Administration or related field. 3 -5 years of experience in student conduct with demonstrated progressive responsibility. Demonstrated training and/or experience in the investigation and adjudication of Title IX cases. Prior supervisory experience. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Additional Qualifications: Experience working with Maxient or related software programs. Demonstrated ability to solve complex issues while functioning as an independent decision-maker. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Higher Education Administration or related field. Experience using mediation and/or restorative justice as a conflict resolution model. Demonstrated experience in strategic planning and assessment. Experience as a member of a behavioral assessment/intervention team. Knowledge of principles and procedures involved in risk assessment. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205812 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). Applicants may also submit documentation of relevant training, certifications, licenses, or professional development experiences that support their qualifications for this position. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205598": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni Engagement and Executive Director of the Alumni Association",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Director of Alumni Engagement and Executive Director of the Alumni Association SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Director of Alumni Engagement and Executive Director of the Alumni Association Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Alumni Engagement and Executive Director of the Alumni Association Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Alumni Engagement Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $95,000.00 - $100,000.00 Position ID: 205598 Share Job Description: Lead engagement for a community of 76,000 alumni and help shape the future of SUNY Oneonta. As the Director of Alumni Engagement and Executive Director of the Alumni Association , you will provide strategic leadership for alumni communications, programs, and events while overseeing initiatives that strengthen lifelong connections to the university. This role offers the opportunity to collaborate with more than 100 alumni volunteers, and advance institutional priorities through meaningful relationship-building, mentoring the next generation of student leaders, and volunteer engagement. Reporting to the Vice President for University Advancement and Executive Director of the SUNY Oneonta Foundation, the successful candidate will join a collaborative leadership team dedicated to fostering engagement, philanthropy, and pride across the SUNY Oneonta community. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneontaalumni.com/ . Duties May Include: Alumni Engagement Developing and sustaining relationships with alumni at the local, regional, and national levels. Planning and executing alumni programs and events that promote engagement, pride, and lifelong connections to SUNY Oneonta, including Alumni Weekend, Alumni of Distinction, regional gatherings, affinity programs, and alumni-student networking opportunities. Promoting student awareness of alumni resources and encouraging student participation in engagement activities and networking programs. Communications & Marketing Serving as Managing Editor of Reflections, the SUNY Oneonta Alumni Association magazine. Directing alumni communications across digital, print, email, and web platforms. Coordinating alumni and advancement messaging and providing updates to the Alumni Association Board of Directors and alumni community. Data Management & Operations Ensuring the accuracy and integrity of alumni records and constituent data. Maximizing the effective use of Blackbaud Raiser's Edge and other constituent relationship management systems. Maintaining and enhancing alumni biographical, contact, and career information through surveys, outreach, and data collection initiatives. Evaluating processes and conducting operational analyses to improve efficiency and effectiveness. Leadership & Administration Supervising four professional staff members, two administrative assistants, and student employees. Administering alumni recognition programs, including nomination processes, committee coordination, and event execution. Recruiting, supporting, and engaging alumni volunteers and ambassadors. Overseeing budgets, contracts, financial management, and strategic planning for alumni engagement and association operations. Alumni Association Board Relations Fostering effective partnerships between the Alumni Association Board and the university community. Coordinating board and committee meetings, including agenda development, reporting, and follow-up. Leading board member recruitment, onboarding, and development efforts. Supporting collaboration between the Alumni Association Board and the SUNY Oneonta Foundation. Salary: $95,000 - $100,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Experience in Alumni Relations, Advancement, or a related field. Leadership experience in supervising, developing, and/or evaluating staff. Demonstrated ability to design and implement strategic initiatives, programs, and/or engagement activities. Demonstrated strong communication and interpersonal skills. Additional Qualifications: Experience managing data, ensuring record accuracy, and generating reports. Experience coordinating events or facilitating meetings. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree. Five years of experience in Alumni Relations, University Advancement, Donor Relations, or related field. Demonstrated experience in volunteer management, board relations, stakeholder engagement, and event or program leadership. Experience working with alumni engagement platforms, Blackbaud Raiser's Edge, CRM systems, or other related database management platforms. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/mission-values-vision/inclusivity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=205598#pageTop . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204531": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor and PRODiG+ Fellow of Clinical, Counseling, or Applied Psychology",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor and PRODiG+ Fellow of Clinical, Counseling, or Applied Psychology SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Visiting Assistant Professor and PRODiG+ Fellow of Clinical, Counseling, or Applied Psychology Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Visiting Assistant Professor and PRODiG+ Fellow of Clinical, Counseling, or Applied Psychology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Psychology Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Sep 4, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $65,000.00 - $65,000.00 Position ID: 204531 Share Job Description: SUNY Oneonta is proud to be a member of the SUNY Promoting Recruitment, Opportunity, Diversity, Inclusion and Growth Plus ( PRODiG+ ) Fellowship Program, PRODiG+ is an initiative of SUNY system aiming to (1) increase the number and share of excellent diverse faculty committed to advancing the ideals of diversity, equity, and inclusion; and (2) strengthen the pipeline for retention and support of those faculty. Through these efforts, we aim to enhance the richness of our academic environment and further contribute to the sustained merit of the SUNY system of institutions. Join us on this exciting venture, where excellence meets inclusivity. Additional information on the PRODiG+ Fellowship can be found at https://www.suny.edu/prodig-plus/ . The Department of Psychology at the State University of New York at Oneonta invites applications for a PRODiG+ Fellowship beginning Spring 2027. The fellowship is for a 12-month appointment for two years. The fellowship is expected to transition into a tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor of Clinical, Counseling, or Applied (clinical focus) Psychology after two years, provided the fellow achieves performance milestones during this period. This position reports directly to the Chair of the Department of Psychology. The Department of Psychology at the State University of New York at Oneonta is a thriving department of ten full-time faculty members with diverse research interests that create an engaging learning environment characterized by accessible faculty, teamwork, student research opportunities, and technology-supported classrooms. The department is committed to providing a solid knowledge base in psychology, fostering scientific inquiry and critical thinking skills, promoting competence in written and oral communication, and supporting ethical and social responsibility in a diverse world. We value experience working with diverse populations, inclusive teaching pedagogies, and multicultural teaching experiences that support students' overall professional development. The department is part of the School of Sciences, which consists of 10 academic departments and nearly 2,000 students majoring in 20 programs. To learn more about the University and the Department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ and https://suny.oneonta.edu/psychology . Duties include but are not limited to: Teach a reduce course load (two courses in fall and spring, totaling 12 credit hours for the academic year) in clinical psychology and develop courses in area of specialization. Have an active research program. Participate in student involvements such as advisement, research supervision, and mentoring. Participate in PRODiG+ programing on campus and SUNY-wide. Provide service to the department and university. Salary: $65,000. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Must be eligible to work in the United States without a visa sponsorship. Additional information on the PRODiG+ Fellowship Benefits can be found at https://www.suny.edu/prodig-plus/ . Requirements: Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: To participate in PRODiG+, candidates are required to: Be eligible to work in the United States without a visa sponsorship. Have a doctorate degree in Clinical, Counseling, or Applied (clinical focus) Psychology, or a closely related discipline. ABD considered; official confirmation of degree conferral by issuing institution by start of employment. Demonstrate personal, academic, and/or work experience engaging with diversity, equity, and inclusion and/or a commitment to facilitating and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Such experience may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/unpaid/community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience offering clinical, health, and social service-related courses. Can potentially contribute to our applied experiential learning opportunities is highly desired (e.g., community outreach, evidence-based interventions with non-profits, service-learning, etc.). Ability to teach courses in our core areas of our curriculum. Evidence of: teaching effectiveness, capability of initiating a suitable and productive research program, and scholarly productivity. Demonstrated experience involving undergraduate students in research. Experience advising and mentoring undergraduate students. Experience in teaching, mentoring, research, or service with diverse and/or multicultural populations. Preference will be given to candidates who are: Current SUNY students, alumni, and/or Fellows. From a low-income background (e.g., Pell-eligible as undergraduates), were first-generation college students (students whose parents have not earned a bachelor's degree), have overcome adversity, are AmeriCorps alumni, or are veterans. Candidates must submit a response to the following essay prompt, in 750 words or less: Please describe how you've engaged, facilitated, and/or enhanced diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Examples should include personal, academic, and/or work experience and may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/unpaid/community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations. Additional Information: The PRODiG+ Fellowship is open to any and all prospective candidates regardless of race, color, national origin, or sex, and is consistent with all current governing federal and state nondiscrimination law. All application submissions will be assessed and evaluated in according with the required eligibility criteria. SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204531 Please upload letter of interest, curriculum vitae, transcripts, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research interests, and your response to the essay prompt listed above. Please include course evaluations if available. Contact information for three references must be provided; one reference must be able to comment on teaching effectiveness; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=201581": {
      "title": "Associate Professor and Director: Master of Social Work Program",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Associate Professor and Director: Master of Social Work Program SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Associate Professor and Director: Master of Social Work Program Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Professor and Director: Master of Social Work Program Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Human Ecology Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Jun 16, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Position ID: 201581 Share Job Description: Job Description: SUNY Oneonta seeks a MSW Program Director/Field Education Administrator to support the development of our newly created online Master of Social Work program, beginning in January 2027. Expectations include, but are not limited to program administration, teaching, research, student advisement, service to the school, university, and community, and continuing professional development. Key responsibilities include: Serving as Program Director for the Master of Social Work Program. Providing leadership in program administration, development, and ongoing operations. Representing the MSW program as the primary liaison to the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE). Coordinating and directing the program's CSWE accreditation process. Teaching 2-4 courses across the undergraduate Human Development & Family Studies program and the MSW program, while supporting student success. Advising MSW students on academic progress and career pathways. Recruiting and retaining students within the MSW program. Engaging in university, departmental, and program service. Participating in scholarly, professional, and continuing development activities. This is a 10-month, in-person appointment with a reduced teaching load while serving as Program Director. A summer stipend is included. Additional duties include but are not limited to: Program Director Leadership within the MSW and HDFS in collaboration with Department Chair Develop a shared vision and strategic plan that coordinates with the University goals. Coordinate course scheduling calendar year-round, facilitate advising, and oversee curriculum and field placements. Oversee CSWE and state regulatory requirements for MSW accreditation and licensure. Implement transparent communication and advocacy within and outside the MSW program and HDFS. Build and support capacity that will advance education, research, and outreach. Identify practical approaches for faculty, staff, and student retention, engagement, and satisfaction. Facilitate professional development for faculty, staff, and graduate students. Field Education Leadership Provide strategic leadership and overall management of the MSW field education program, including planning, coordination, implementation, and evaluation. Develop, maintain, and strengthen partnerships with community agencies, field instructors, and professional organizations. Oversee the placement process, including matching students with field sites that meet educational goals and CSWE competencies. Ensure compliance with CSWE accreditation standards, field education policies, and university requirements. Supervise and support field liaisons, faculty field instructors, and staff involved in field education. Design and deliver field orientation, training, and professional development for students and agency supervisors. Salary: $80,000 - $90,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits. Requirements: Required Qualifications: MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. Minimum of five (5) years of post-MSW social work practice experience. Prior college-level teaching experience. Demonstrated experience in social work field education, supervision, or program administration. Strong understanding of CSWE accreditation standards and field education requirements. Demonstrated academic experience sufficient to qualify for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate in Social Work or a related field. Experience as department head or program director. Experience with assessment and accreditation/reaccreditation processes. Demonstrated experience in maximizing faculty, staff, and student professional growth and potential. Demonstrated efforts to increase student access and success. Knowledge of online program planning, curriculum development, and monitoring students' academic progress. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and culturally responsive social work education. Experience developing and managing community partnerships. Evidence of leadership, innovation, and program development in field education. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70- plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=201581 . Please upload a curriculum vitae, letter of interest and a statement of higher education administrative experience or supervisory experience. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/aboutoneonta/employment Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200704": {
      "title": "Physician Assistant Program Director",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Physician Assistant Program Director SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Physician Assistant Program Director Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Physician Assistant Program Director Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Sciences Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: May 19, 2026 Type: Full-time Position ID: 200704 Share Job Description: The School of Sciences at SUNY Oneonta is seeking a Physician Assistant (PA) Program Director to lead the development and implementation of its new Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) program. This is a unique opportunity for a visionary and dynamic leader to establish and shape a new PA program from the ground up while building a lasting impact within the university and broader community. This position offers a primarily academic work environment with clinical and community engagement. The majority of responsibilities are administrative and leadership-focused (approximately 50%), complemented by teaching and service (30%) and clinical practice (20%), with the expectation of maintaining clinical currency. This is a 12-month appointment , with occasional travel required for conferences, clinical site development, and accreditation activities, as well as extended hours during key periods. In this role, the Director will engage in teaching, clinical care activities, and university and public service, while ensuring compliance with SUNY and NYSED requirements and ARC-PA accreditation standards. The successful candidate will qualify for appointment as a clinical faculty member and will play a critical role in building a high-quality, student-centered program that prepares future PAs to serve diverse communities with excellence and compassion. Duties include but are not limited to: Program Leadership and Administration Providing strategic and operational leadership for the PA program. Supervising faculty and staff, including the medical director. Overseeing program operations, budgeting, and alignment with institutional goals. Curriculum Development and Assessment Developing and implementing a rigorous, innovative, and outcomes-based curriculum. Integrating simulation and interprofessional education. Establishing policies for admissions, progression, and graduation. Accreditation and Compliance Guiding and managing approval process through SUNY and NYSED. Leading ARC-PA accreditation processes and ensuring ongoing compliance. Preparing accreditation documentation and remaining informed on standards. Faculty and Staff Recruitment and Development Recruiting qualified, diverse faculty and staff. Supervising and mentoring principal faculty, instructional faculty, and program staff. Fostering a collaborative, inclusive academic culture. Encouraging scholarly activity while not requiring it as the primary driver for promotion or advancement. Student Recruitment and Success Directing the admissions process to attract a qualified and diverse student body. Supporting student academic advising, mentoring, and wellness. Teaching in areas of expertise. Community Engagement and Advocacy Building partnerships with Bassett Healthcare Network and with other clinical affiliates and healthcare organizations. Representing and advocating for the program locally and nationally. Seeking philanthropic and grant support. Salary : $130,000 - $145,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Graduate of an ARC-PA-accredited PA program. Current NCCPA certification. Eligible for or currently licensed as a PA in New York State. At least three years of clinical experience as a PA. Minimum of two years of academic experience in a PA or healthcare-related program. Preferred: Doctoral degree (e.g., DMSc, DHSc, PhD, EdD, MD, DO). Excellent communication and organizational abilities. Over three years of academic leadership or teaching in PA or health professions education. Knowledge of rural/underserved healthcare delivery. Ability to build and sustain clinical and community partnerships. Familiarity with ARC-PA standards and program development. Experience with state or federal grants (e.g., HRSA, SAMHSA). Strong leadership, team-building, and strategic planning skills. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=200704 . Please upload a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, copies of transcripts, statement of teaching philosophy, and a brief vision statement for developing an innovative and student-centered MSPAS program. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204050": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Sport Management",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Sport Management SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor - Sport Management Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor - Sport Management Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Sport & Exercise Science Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Aug 24, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $60,000.00 - $62,000.00 Position ID: 204050 Share Job Description: The Department of Sport and Exercise Sciences at the State University of New York at Oneonta is seeking an Assistant Professor - Sport Management to support a growing department. Expectations include, but are not limited to, teaching, research, student advisement, university service, and continuing professional development. The Department of Sport and Exercise Sciences proudly offers majors in four academic programs: the Exercise Science Major, Sports Management Major, Athletic Coaching minor, and Sports Management minor, with a thriving community of over 400 students and a forward- looking approach to further curriculum development. As we continue to expand, the University is demonstrating its commitment to preparing a new generation of aspiring sport health professionals by adding six tenure track positions. Through practical assignments and discussions of current issues, students learn how sport management and exercise science impacts us on a local, regional, and global scale. The Sport Management and Exercise Science classes use a wide array of facilities, including enhanced classrooms, equipped with current teaching modalities that allow for strong interaction between faculty and students. Sport Management and Exercise Science classes may also use many of our campus fitness and recreation facilities. To delve deeper into the University and explore the opportunities within our department visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ and https://suny.oneonta.edu/sport-and-exercise-sciences . Duties include but are not limited to: Teach required courses in the department. Advise students. Participate in department service. Have a research agenda. Contribute to the positive ethos of the department. Appreciate DEISJ (Diversity: Equity, Inclusion, and Social Justice) throughout courses and interactions with students. Teach other courses to meet department needs. Sport Management courses in the curriculum include the following. Candidates need not be proficient in all of them. Introduction to Sport Management. Misconceptions and Representations in Sport (DEI focus). Sport Marketing. Sport and American Society (DEI focus). Leadership in Sport Management. Resource Management in Sport. Legal Issues in Sport. Critiquing Contemporary Themes in Sport (Senior Capstone, DEI focus). Sport Promotion and Sales. Sport Facility. Esports. Sport Communication. Event Management in Sport. Sport Analytics. Governance and Policy in Sport. Women in Sport (DEI focus). The Media and Sports (DEI focus). Other courses of interest. Base Salary: $60,000 - $62,000. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Requirements: Required Qualifications: Doctorate in sport management or related field. ABD considered; official confirmation of degree conferral by issuing institution by start of employment. Preferred: Commitment to providing academic advising. A desire to work collaboratively across the department and institution. An appreciation for DEISJ. Experience teaching undergraduates at the college level. Willingness to develop courses building on the current curricula and future expansion. Ability to establish a research program that mentors and engages undergraduate students. Experience working with diverse populations and/or teaching pedagogies and/ or multicultural teaching experience. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=204050 . Please upload letter of interest, curriculum vitae, transcripts, and statement of teaching philosophy. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204223": {
      "title": "Coordinator of the Center for Community College Partnerships",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Coordinator of the Center for Community College Partnerships SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Coordinator of the Center for Community College Partnerships Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Coordinator of the Center for Community College Partnerships Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Enrollment Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $67,500.00 - $69,000.00 Position ID: 204223 Share Job Description: The Center for Community College Partnerships at SUNY Oneonta invites applications for the position of Coordinator of the Center for Community College Partnerships (CCCP). Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Strategic Enrollment, the successful candidate will play a pivotal role partnering with community colleges to strengthen transfer pathways, advance articulation agreements, and support transfer student transition and success. This position will focus on developing, implementing, and sustaining initiatives that create seamless transfer pathways, strengthen articulation agreements, and enhance the academic success, persistence, and degree completion of transfer students. Additionally, the Coordinator will serve as a resource to SUNY Oneonta faculty and staff by providing training, guidance, and support on best practices for supporting transfer students, fostering faculty collaborations, and promoting student success. To learn more about the University please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/. Duties include but are not limited to: Establishing, cultivating, and maintaining strong relationships with community college partners, faculty, advisors, and administrators. Coordinating efforts to establish dual admissions programs with targeted NYS Community Colleges. Planning and executing both on and off campus events with partner institutions that support transfer student enrollment. Preparing reports to evaluate the effectiveness of partnership programs and recommend improvements. Reviewing transfer pathways from community colleges, identify challenges and collaborate to develop solutions. Collaborating with both academic and support service departments to develop programming that facilitates and supports transfer student enrollment and success. Providing training, guidance, and resources to faculty and staff on best practices for supporting transfer students, fostering faculty collaborations, and promoting student success. Traveling to community colleges and partner organizations to support relationship-building, outreach efforts, and transfer initiatives. Participating in occasional evening and weekend programs, events, and recruitment activities as needed. Salary: $67,500 - $69,000 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. Minimum of five years of experience in higher education. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Demonstrated organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines. Knowledge of transfer processes, articulation agreements, and community college systems. Preferred: Master's degree. Five years of experience in enrollment management, academic affairs, student services, transfer services, or related areas within higher education. Experience working directly with community colleges, transfer students, or transfer-focused programs. Proficiency with student information systems (e.g., Banner) and CRM platforms. Experience coordinating events, outreach programs, or delivering presentations. Knowledge of SUNY policies and procedures. Experience working with and serving diverse populations, including a commitment to inclusion and equity through engagement with students, faculty, staff, and community partners from a variety of backgrounds. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204223 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website