    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204220": {
      "title": "Associate Director for Graduate Admissions",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Associate Director for Graduate Admissions SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director for Graduate Admissions Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director for Graduate Admissions Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Enrollment Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Aug 28, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $67,000.00 - $68,500.00 Position ID: 204220 Share Job Description: The Associate Director for Graduate Admissions plays a vital role in advancing SUNY Oneonta's graduate enrollment goals by leading recruitment and enrollment efforts for the university's graduate programs serving domestic, international, and online students. This position is responsible for developing and implementing recruitment strategies, cultivating prospective student relationships, coordinating admissions processes, and promoting graduate opportunities through outreach, events, and partnerships. The Associate Director serves as a key contributor to enrollment growth and student success while supporting the mission of the university. Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Strategic Enrollment, the Associate Director joins a dedicated team committed to serving students and their families. This position participates in and coordinates activities, events, and programs that promote the university's graduate offerings and is responsible for student recruitment, coordination of the admissions application and review process, and follow-up activities in support of graduate enrollment goals. The successful candidate will join a dedicated team committed to serving students and their families. We value inclusivity and are committed to the recruitment and enrollment of a diverse student body. This position is open to a hybrid work structure and will require working days on campus. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit https://suny.oneonta.edu/ or https://suny.oneonta.edu/admissions . Duties include but are not limited to: Representing the University professionally and ethically at recruiting events, conferences, and meetings and traveling independently to support recruitment and enrollment efforts. Assisting with the development of graduate recruitment strategies targeting external audiences and current SUNY Oneonta students. Researching and identifying target markets and recruiting venues, analyzing trends, and assessing the effectiveness of recruitment activities and events. Utilizing innovative recruitment techniques and marketing methods to develop, plan, organize, and execute recruitment initiatives. Employing effective and professional communication and marketing practices to generate and respond to inquiries, provide consistent recruiting information, and communicate proactively with external agencies, partner universities, school districts, and private-sector organizations. Delivering presentations to diverse audiences in both in-person and virtual settings. Implementing effective practices for coordinating and reviewing applications, including managing documents, maintaining student relationship management processes, and supporting application review activities. Working proficiently within the Slate Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system to manage prospective student communications, track recruitment activities, and support enrollment objectives. Salary: $67,000 - $68,500 commensurate with experience. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college/university. Minimum of five years of experience working in college admissions or a similar setting. Excellent customer service, interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills. Valid driver's license. Ability to travel and work evenings and weekends. Experience and proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and demonstrated ability to learn and use technology effectively, including social media and other electronic systems. Familiarity with undergraduate and graduate school application processes. Additional: Experience developing and delivering presentations to prospective students, community organizations, or other audiences. Experience analyzing and utilizing data, reports, or metrics to support recruitment, admissions, enrollment, or organizational decision-making. Preferred: Master's degree from an accredited college/university. Previous experience in graduate admissions. Experience with Slate, university systems, or other similar CRM or student information systems. Demonstrated success leveraging technology, data, analytics, or innovative recruitment strategies to achieve recruitment, enrollment, or organizational goals. Demonstrated initiative and achievement in meeting goals, improving processes, or advancing organizational objectives. Demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity. Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle . Application Instructions: To apply online go to: https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204220 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment. . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=200743": {
      "title": "HR Generalist",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: HR Generalist SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: HR Generalist Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details HR Generalist Category: Management / Confidential Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Employee Services Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: May 20, 2026 Type: Full-time Position ID: 200743 Share Job Description: Employee Services plays a vital role in the everyday success of organizations, and at SUNY Oneonta, that impact is felt across every corner of campus. SUNY Oneonta invites applications for an HR Generalist within the Employee Services Department. This is an opportunity to join a collaborative, service-driven team dedicated to supporting our employees. We thrive by bringing together individuals with diverse perspectives, experiences, and strengths who work toward a shared goal. In this role, you will serve as both a member of the campus Employee Services team and a point of contact for the SUNY Research Foundation (RF) and RF employees working at SUNY Oneonta. This unique position supports a wide range of HR functions while contributing to research-driven and departmental initiatives that have meaningful impact across the university. Employee Services at SUNY Oneonta is committed to providing comprehensive human resources support that fosters a positive, inclusive, and efficient workplace environment. The department partners closely with campus leadership, faculty, and staff to deliver services related to recruitment, onboarding, benefits, and employee engagement. This role is unique in that it supports the SUNY Research Foundation (RF), a private, nonprofit organization that administers externally funded grants and contracts for SUNY, while remaining embedded within the Employee Services team. This dual partnership offers a dynamic opportunity to work across systems and stakeholders to support research-driven initiatives and the employees who make them possible. To learn more about the University, the department, and the Research Foundation, please visit: https://suny.oneonta.edu/ . https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/university-offices/employee-services . https://www.rfsuny.org/About-Us/ . Duties include but are not limited to: Managing SUNY Research Foundation employee processes: Conducting orientations for new hires. Maintaining accurate employee records in ORACLE. Managing and monitoring compliance with the RF Affirmative Action Plan. Conducting thorough background checks, including criminal, reference, and credit checks as required by program needs. Serving as the RF IT security contact. Maintaining the HR portion of the Research, Grants, and Contracts website and intranet. Collaborating with Employee Services team members, SUNY RF, and the Office of Research, Grants and Contracts to assist with developing job descriptions, conducting searches, and administering benefits, leaves, and employee relations activities. Ensuring compliance with federal and state policies. Assisting in the preparation of employment action notices, such as pay increase notification letters. Providing guidance to employees regarding benefits, including health insurance, retirement, and leaves. Gathering data and compiling reports for compliance activities and institutional data requests. Developing and maintaining content for the Employee Services website and intranet, and creating informational materials and forms to support HR processes and initiatives. Participating actively in the Employee Services team, including identifying short- and long-range plans for onboarding and orientation initiatives. Collaborating with Employee Services team members and leadership to create and support training and development opportunities. Supporting process improvement efforts by identifying and implementing automated HR systems. Occasionally supervising student employees. Salary: $55,000. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. A minimum of one year of professional work experience. Excellent interpersonal and customer service skills. Proficiency in Microsoft products such as Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint and TEAMS. Familiarity with web design/maintenance or ability to learn. Additional: Working knowledge of federal and state employment laws. Ability to extract and analyze data, compose and present comprehensive reports. Demonstrated support of an inclusive and welcoming workplace or environment. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Preferred: Knowledge of and experience with varied human resource information systems. Ability to develop informational materials and design presentation materials. Experience working in the Human Resources field. Experience working with and serving diverse populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/diversity . Moreover, the University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=200743 . Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references (required). For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    },
    "https://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=206202": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Human Development and Family Studies",
      "description": "SUNY Oneonta\nJob Posting: Lecturer of Human Development and Family Studies SUNY Oneonta \n\tJob Posting: Lecturer of Human Development and Family Studies Title Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Lecturer of Human Development and Family Studies Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Human Ecology Locations: Oneonta, NY Posted: Oct 27, 2026 Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $52,838.00 - $52,838.00 Position ID: 206202 Share Job Description: Every individual, family, and community is shaped by relationships, experiences, and opportunities across the lifespan. As a Lecturer in Human Development and Family Studies at the State University of New York at Oneonta, you'll help prepare the next generation of professionals dedicated to improving quality of life through education, advocacy, and human services beginning fall 2027. This 10-month academic-year appointment offers the opportunity to enjoy the balance of the academic calendar while benefiting from New York's public higher education system, including comprehensive health, dental, vision, and retirement benefits. Just as importantly, you'll play a vital role in shaping future professionals whose work will support individuals, families, and communities for years to come. Through engaging instruction, mentorship, and experiential learning opportunities, you'll help bring that mission to life. In the Human Development and Family Studies (HDFS) program, students explore the factors that shape individuals, families, and communities across the lifespan while engaging in applied coursework, internships, and hands-on learning experiences that connect theory to practice and prepare them for careers in human services or graduate study. To learn more about the University and the department, please visit: https://suny.oneonta.edu/ https://suny.oneonta.edu/human-ecology https://suny.oneonta.edu/academics/schools/education-human-ecology-and-sports-studies Duties May Include: Teaching a variety of undergraduate courses, including: Human Development Marriage and Family Relationships Parent Education Teaching courses aligned with your area of expertise. Holding office hours and providing support to students. Salary : $52,838. SUNY Oneonta is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness qualifying employer. Information on SUNY's comprehensive benefits offerings can be found at https://www.suny.edu/benefits . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Human Development and Family Studies, Developmental Psychology, or a closely related field. Experience teaching college-level courses. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. or comparable degree. More than one year of college-level teaching experience. Experience teaching face-to-face classes. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: Substance Use Gerontology Program Development Early Childhood Experience working with or serving a diverse and/or multicultural populations. Additional Information: SUNY Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully.  Oneonta enrolls about 5,500 students who pursue bachelor's or master's degrees or certificates in one of 70-plus academic programs. Known as an exemplary residential campus that values inclusion, service and sustainability, SUNY Oneonta is a nurturing community where students grow intellectually, thrive socially, and live purposefully. The university is located in the City of Oneonta, nestled in the northern foothills of the Catskill Mountains about a four-hour drive from New York City, Boston, and Philadelphia. With a population just shy of 14,000, Oneonta is one of the 20 Most Picturesque Small Towns in America, according to Microsoft News. The natural beauty of the region is breathtaking year-round. Each season offers outdoor activities such as hiking, biking, boating, swimming, and skiing. Employees give SUNY Oneonta high marks for work/life balance, management, and culture. The university's indeed.com rating is 4.4, with one recent review noting that the people are what make SUNY Oneonta so special. SUNY Oneonta values a diverse university community. Please visit our website on diversity at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about/mission-values-vision/inclusivity . Moreover, the university is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. Women, persons of color, persons with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. \"At SUNY Oneonta, we believe that diversity is an asset and a source of strength that energizes our collective growth and innovation.\" - President Alberto Cardelle. Application Instructions: To apply online go to: http://oneonta.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=206202 . Please upload a curriculum vitae and letter of interest. Contact information for three references must be provided; instructions for submitting letters of reference will be sent directly to the referees. For other employment and regional opportunities, please visit our website at: https://suny.oneonta.edu/about-oneonta/employment . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Oneonta 108 Ravine Parkway, Oneonta, NY 13820"
    }
